from bank import add
add('B01',[('Workflow','Application code defines the sequence and decision gates.'),('Agent','The system chooses a next action from observations within application-enforced limits.'),('Task boundary','The explicit user, input, output and actions excluded from the release.')],('A policy assistant is asked to issue a refund. Its release scope allows only cited drafts. What should happen?','Draft the policy answer and route the action request to the named human reviewer.','Add a refund tool because the user requested it.','Treat a confident model answer as approval.','A new request does not expand the application’s authorized effects. Keep the read-only boundary intact.'),'Compare a fixed retrieve-then-draft workflow with an agent loop for your own repetitive task. What observed failure would justify a loop?')
add('B02',[('Virtual environment','An isolated Python interpreter environment with its own installed dependencies.'),('Reproducibility','Another person can run the project from declared files and setup steps.'),('Secret boundary','Credentials remain outside tracked code, fixtures, logs and learner notes.')],('Your project runs only when launched from your editor. Which check provides useful evidence?','Run the documented command from a fresh shell and a newly created environment.','Copy your entire home directory into the project.','Install dependencies globally until the import error disappears.','A fresh environment exposes undeclared packages and working-directory assumptions.'),'Which two assumptions in your setup would fail on a colleague’s machine, and how will you test each?')
add('B03',[('Evaluation case','An input with an expected behavior and the evidence supporting that expectation.'),('Holdout set','Cases reserved for a final comparison and not used to tune the current system.'),('Label ambiguity','A case whose expected outcome needs clarification rather than a forced confident label.')],('You inspect a holdout failure and change the prompt specifically to fix it. How should you describe that case?','It has informed development and is no longer untouched holdout evidence.','It remains untouched because the question text did not change.','Delete the failure and report the remaining holdout score.','Using a case to tune behavior changes its role, even when the stored text is identical.'),'Write an answerable and an unanswerable question with nearly identical vocabulary. What evidence distinguishes their labels?')
add('B04',[('Output contract','Allowed fields, types, statuses and invariants checked before a response is used.'),('Citation integrity','Referenced source IDs must exist in the selected evidence set.'),('Factual support','A cited passage must actually establish the answer’s claim.')],('A response is valid JSON and cites a real passage, but invents an exception. Which judgment is justified?','Structural checks passed, but factual support still failed.','The answer is verified because the citation ID exists.','JSON validation can prove the policy exception is true.','Syntax and reference membership cannot establish that a passage entails a claim.'),'Design one malformed output and one well-formed but unsupported output. Explain the different checks needed.')
add('B05',[('Provider adapter','A narrow interface that translates provider-specific calls and errors into application contracts.'),('Transient failure','A temporary error that may be eligible for a bounded retry.'),('Overall deadline','The maximum elapsed time across attempts, waits and processing for a request.')],('A provider rejects a request because credentials lack permission. What is the best default retry behavior?','Fail clearly without repeated attempts and keep the user’s draft input.','Retry indefinitely until permission changes.','Silently send the same private prompt to another provider.','A permission failure is not normally corrected by repeating the request; fallback also changes data routing.'),'Specify which fake failures you will retry, maximum attempts, total deadline, and what the user sees when those limits are reached.')
add('B06',[('Context budget','A bounded allocation for instructions, question, source metadata, passages and output.'),('Traceable truncation','Omissions are recorded while source identity and meaningful conditions are retained.'),('Token estimate','An approximation that must not be reported as measured provider usage.')],('The next sentence after a selected passage excludes opened products. Your budget cuts it off. What should you do?','Select a complete condition with its exception or return a scoped limitation.','Answer from the positive sentence alone.','Remove the source ID to save space.','Cutting a rule’s exception can reverse its meaning. Evidence selection must preserve the decision boundary.'),'How would you compare one, three and five passages without confusing extra length with better evidence?')
add('B07',[('Source revision','A specific version of a document with a stable identity and content hash.'),('Ingestion state','An explicit stage such as received, parsed, indexed or failed.'),('Active policy','The source revision selected under a documented effective-date rule.')],('A new shipping policy contradicts the previous version. How should current queries select evidence?','Use the active revision and retain the older version as identifiable historical evidence.','Mix both versions without dates so the model chooses.','Overwrite the old file and erase all revision metadata.','Current and historical policy questions need explicit source lifecycle rules.'),'Draw the state transitions for a file accepted by upload but rejected during parsing. What must the interface avoid claiming?')
add('B08',[('Chunk','A retrievable section that retains enough context to interpret its rule.'),('Lexical retrieval','Ranking using word or term overlap rather than semantic meaning.'),('Recall at k','The fraction of relevant gold passage IDs retrieved among the first k results; no-source cases need separate scoring.')],('A lexical retriever misses “delivery” when the relevant text says “shipping.” What does this establish?','A vocabulary mismatch in this baseline that needs a controlled comparison.','The policy contains no answer under any retrieval method.','Adding more agents will necessarily fix retrieval.','A lexical failure identifies a concrete limitation; it does not prove the evidence is absent.'),'Create a chunk boundary that loses an exception. Then redesign it and show how the retrieved evidence changes.')
add('B09',[('Grounded answer','A draft whose factual claims are supported by the evidence available for that run.'),('Clarification','A request for missing user information that changes how a rule applies.'),('Abstention','An explicit inability to establish an answer from the available sources.')],('The policy covers unopened items, but the question does not say whether the item was opened. What fits best?','Ask for item condition before determining eligibility.','Assume unopened because it is more helpful.','Approve the return with a high confidence percentage.','Missing applicability information calls for clarification, not an invented assumption.'),'Write one clarification and one abstention for your policy collection. What is missing in each case?')
add('B10',[('Tool contract','Validated inputs, outputs, side effects, permissions and failure behavior for an operation.'),('Owner scope','Access derived from the authenticated user’s authority rather than a model-supplied identity.'),('Allowlisted dispatch','Only explicitly registered operation names can be invoked.')],('A model supplies another tenant’s order ID to an allowed lookup tool. Which layer must reject unauthorized access?','The tool’s server-side ownership check.','The wording of the model’s apology.','The tool description alone.','An allowed tool can still receive unauthorized arguments; identity and authority must be enforced in code.'),'Design a safe lookup result that omits unnecessary customer fields. Which fields do you exclude and why?')
add('B11',[('Agent state','Structured application data recording observed results and the current stage.'),('Transition','An explicitly permitted movement between states.'),('Step limit','An application-enforced maximum number of iterations independent of model instructions.')],('The agent requests the same unhelpful lookup repeatedly. What should the application do?','Stop at the configured bound and preserve the observed trace.','Keep running until the model declares success.','Invent a tool result so the loop can terminate.','Bounded termination is enforced by the application, and an observed failure must not become fictional success.'),'Specify an invalid transition in your state machine and a test that rejects it even when the model requests it.')
add('B12',[('Bound approval','Human authorization tied to exact arguments, owner, revision and expiry.'),('Idempotency key','A scoped identifier used to recognize a repeated operation without duplicating its effect.'),('Uncertain outcome','A remote action may have occurred, but local evidence cannot yet confirm the result.')],('A reviewer approves a draft ticket update, then its arguments change. Can the changed action execute under the old approval?','No; the new arguments need a new bound approval.','Yes; approval applies to all future edits.','Yes; using the same idempotency key authorizes it.','Duplicate handling does not authorize changed effects; approval must identify the actual proposed action.'),'Describe how you would reconcile a timeout after a remote service may already have performed the action.')
add('B13',[('Request validation','Enforcing required fields, sizes, types and allowed values at the API boundary.'),('Server identity','The authenticated principal established independently of client-supplied owner fields.'),('Accepted versus complete','A received request or queued job is not necessarily a finished result.')],('A client adds owner_id for another account to a draft request. What should the API do?','Derive ownership from authentication and reject or ignore the untrusted owner field.','Trust the field because the request is valid JSON.','Ask the model whether the owner is legitimate.','Input structure is not proof of authority. Ownership comes from the server-established identity.'),'Write success and failure response examples for one API route, including a dependency timeout that preserves the draft.')
add('B14',[('Database invariant','A condition backed by constraints, such as unique owner-and-action keys.'),('Transaction','A boundary within which related database changes commit or roll back together.'),('Optional side effect','Work such as model feedback that must not erase already saved user data if it fails.')],('Two requests pass a Python duplicate check at the same time. What protects a unique action key?','A database uniqueness constraint with appropriate transaction handling.','The duplicate check alone.','A note asking users not to click twice.','Concurrent requests can both pass an application precheck; the database must enforce the invariant.'),'Which records in your workflow must commit together, and which remote operation should be represented as a separate observable step?')
add('B15',[('Reviewable draft','An output whose evidence, status and suggested changes are inspectable by the user.'),('Failure recovery UX','A visible error with retained input and an explicit next action.'),('Action status','A label reflecting actual execution state rather than a generated suggestion.')],('A provider times out after a user enters a question. What should the interface preserve?','The question, a clear failure state and an explicit retry path.','An endless loading indicator.','A success label because the request was sent.','A sent request is not a completed draft. Retaining input lets the user recover without inventing success.'),'Plan a usability task that reveals whether a new user understands the difference between a proposed and an executed action.')
add('B16',[('Regression harness','A repeatable run of named cases against a recorded system and dataset revision.'),('Failure denominator','The total relevant cases, including failed or unavailable runs, used to interpret a result.'),('Category analysis','Separate outcomes for groups such as ambiguous, missing-evidence and adversarial cases.')],('Overall pass rate improves while every conflicting-policy case regresses. What should the report show?','Both the aggregate improvement and the conflict-category regression.','Only the overall score.','Remove conflict cases because they are difficult.','An aggregate can conceal a material failure pattern; category-level results preserve the trade-off.'),'Design a report that distinguishes retrieval failures from unsupported generation without hiding unavailable runs.')
add('B17',[('Prompt injection','Untrusted content attempts to redirect the system’s behavior or authority.'),('Trust boundary','A separation where data from one source cannot automatically grant privileges in another.'),('Canary fixture','A synthetic recognizable value used to test unauthorized disclosure without real secrets.')],('A document claims to be a system instruction and requests a private file upload. What prevents the effect?','Application permissions, tool allowlists and data-access checks that the document cannot change.','The document’s confident administrator language.','A model promise to be careful without enforced boundaries.','Retrieved text cannot grant authority. Prompt wording supplements, but cannot replace, permission enforcement.'),'Create an injection test using a real allowed tool name with unauthorized arguments. What must remain protected?')
add('B18',[('Run trace','Structured observations such as stage duration, source revision, tool outcome and retry count.'),('Usage accounting','Separately recording measured provider usage and estimates.'),('Tail latency','The slower end of request durations, which an average can conceal.')],('A timed-out request has no completed answer. How should it appear in metrics?','As a failed run with its elapsed time and failure category.','As a slow success because time was spent.','Excluded from all latency and reliability reports.','Failure and duration are different observations; omitting failures creates a misleading reliability picture.'),'Choose three trace fields that explain an incident without storing private source text or raw provider errors.')
add('B19',[('Container network','A private network where service names resolve for containers, not necessarily for a browser.'),('Persistent volume','Storage that survives removal or replacement of a container.'),('Readiness probe','A check of the dependency needed for the service to fulfill its readiness claim.')],('The API uses db:5432 inside Compose. Which address should the browser normally use in this app?','The public frontend origin with /api proxied to the backend.','db:5432 directly from JavaScript.','The API container’s private filesystem path.','Browser and container network namespaces differ. A same-origin proxy exposes the intended HTTP boundary.'),'Design a restart test that proves a saved record lives in PostgreSQL rather than only in a browser variable.')
add('B20',[('Restore verification','Recovering a backup into an isolated target and checking its actual contents.'),('Rollback boundary','Code rollback and data-schema recovery are distinct operations.'),('Runbook','Concrete diagnosis and recovery steps that another operator can follow.')],('A migration deleted data used by the previous application image. Does rolling back only the image recover it?','No; code rollback cannot recreate deleted data.','Yes; old images always include old database rows.','Yes; restarting the frontend restores the schema.','Images package application code, while database state has its own recovery requirements.'),'Write one recovery instruction with an observable success check and an explicit point where you should stop escalation attempts.')
add('B21',[('Explicit graph','A representation of permitted workflow states and transitions.'),('Durability','Progress survives interruption because required state is persisted outside the process.'),('Architecture baseline','The simpler design against which added complexity is evaluated.')],('A draft must wait two days for approval and survive a process restart. What capability is directly required?','Durable state and a validated resume transition.','Two model personas chatting in memory.','A longer context window alone.','Multiple agents do not make state durable. Persistence and concurrency-safe transitions address the actual requirement.'),'Compare a fixed workflow, loop and durable state machine for one observed capstone failure. Which is the smallest sufficient change?')
add('B22',[('Vertical slice','One complete user path through interface, API, application logic, storage and visible result.'),('Evidence bundle','Inputs, observed outputs, versions, tests and limitations supporting a project claim.'),('Offline baseline','A runnable deterministic path requiring no model credentials or network call.')],('A demo screenshot shows a plausible answer. Which additional check supports a persistence claim?','Save a run, restart the application and retrieve it under the correct account.','Increase the screenshot resolution.','Read the same value from a component variable.','A visual output cannot demonstrate server-side storage or survival across restart.'),'Specify five end-to-end capstone scenarios covering normal, ambiguous, unsupported, unauthorized and unavailable behavior.')
add('B23',[('Peer critique','A reviewer tests the project against explicit criteria and unfamiliar inputs.'),('Disposition','A finding is fixed, deferred or rejected with a recorded reason and owner.'),('Release evidence','Observed behavior for the exact candidate revision and evaluation set.')],('A reviewer finds a cited answer uses an outdated active policy. What is a useful fix-and-verify sequence?','Correct revision selection and rerun current and historical-date cases.','Replace only the demo screenshot.','Delete the reviewer’s question from evaluation.','A source lifecycle defect needs a behavioral fix and regression coverage, not a presentation change.'),'Choose two peer findings and explain how you would prove that the chosen corrections address their actual failure mechanisms.')
add('B24',[('Handover package','Setup, scope, architecture, evaluation, operations and limitations usable without the author present.'),('Scoped claim','A statement of capability limited to the conditions actually tested.'),('Evidence-driven backlog','Future work prioritized from observed defects and user needs with acceptance checks.')],('The project passes 16 of 20 synthetic cases using a fake provider. Which release claim is defensible?','An offline read-only prototype with documented results and remaining failures.','A universally reliable autonomous support service.','A production certification based on the passing cases alone.','The claim must retain dataset size, fake integration boundaries and known limitations.'),'Audit your README for three claims. What artifact supports each, and which claim needs narrowing?')
